  "description": "The 2026 election for Ohio's 4th Congressional District will determine who represents north-central Ohio, including Lima, Marion, and Delaware, in the U.S. House of Representatives. Incumbent Republican Jim Jordan, first elected in 2006 and a prominent conservative leader, seeks re-election in a district with a strong Republican lean (Cook PVI: R+21). He faces Democratic nominee Joshua Kolasinski, a small business owner, and independent candidate Tamie Wilson, an entrepreneur who previously ran as a Democrat in 2022 and 2024. The primary elections took place on May 5, 2026, and the race is rated as 'Solid R' by the Cook Political Report, reflecting the district's entrenched Republican advantage even after mid-decade redistricting.",
